# Parameter definitions for thorn MCNuX

RESTRICTED:

# Self-test battery switch of specs/verification-suite-design.md
# [MCNX-VER-06]: the `unit-selftest` benchmark sets
# MCNuX::run_selftests = yes, which runs the unit self-test battery once at
# initial time and writes one row per named check (measured error, pass flag)
# into the MCNuX::mcnux_selftest grid array. Off by default — the battery is
# verification scaffolding, not part of a production transport run — and
# STEERABLE=NEVER, because the battery's storage and scheduling are decided
# from it at startup.

BOOLEAN run_selftests "Run the MCNuX unit self-test battery at initial time" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Synthetic-event deposition switch of specs/hydro-coupling-source-terms.md
# (the zero-then-add protocol observable, [MCNX-HYD-02]/[MCNX-HYD-03]): the
# `source-zero-add` benchmark sets MCNuX::test_synthetic_deposit = yes, which
# schedules MCNuX_SyntheticDeposit as a contributor in MCNuX_AddToSourceTerms,
# injecting a small deterministic, iteration-scaled event list into fixed
# cells through the [MCNX-HYD-02] ledger arithmetic. Off by default — the
# injection is verification scaffolding, not physics — and STEERABLE=NEVER,
# because the contributor's scheduling is decided from it at startup.

BOOLEAN test_synthetic_deposit "Deposit a synthetic, iteration-scaled event list into the source-term variables each transport step" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Conservation-ledger closure switch of specs/hydro-coupling-source-terms.md
# ([MCNX-HYD-05]; the closure observable of the `source-zero-add` benchmark):
# MCNuX::test_ledger_closure = yes schedules MCNuX_LedgerClosure after all
# contributors of MCNuX_AddToSourceTerms, which checks, per channel
# {P^t, P_x, P_y, P_z, L}, that the grid total Sum_cells (source)*dV*dt
# cancels the event-side packet total dX to relative 1e-13 of the gross event
# activity (eps0-floored), mirrors the verdict table into
# MCNuX::mcnux_ledger_diag, and aborts on any failing channel. Off by default
# — the audit is verification scaffolding, not physics — and STEERABLE=NEVER,
# because the table's storage and the routine's scheduling are decided from
# it at startup. The event side folds the contributors actually active in the
# run: the shared synthetic list (with test_synthetic_deposit) and the
# production emission loop's per-step audit (with enable_emission); the
# grid-side dV*dt multiplier follows the active contributor's own deposit
# normalization, so combining both contributors under the closure is
# forbidden at PARAMCHECK (mcnux_paramcheck.cxx).

BOOLEAN test_ledger_closure "Audit the per-step five-channel conservation-ledger closure of the synthetic event list against the deposited source terms" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Synthetic packet fixture switch of specs/geodesic-propagation.md
# (Verification: flat-spacetime exactness and the Schwarzschild p_t-drift
# study; the `minkowski-freestream` and `schwarzschild-pt` benchmarks):
# MCNuX::test_synthetic_packets = yes seeds a fixed, deterministic set of
# packets at initial time (MCNuX_SeedSyntheticPackets; which set is chosen
# by synthetic_packet_fixture below), schedules the geodesic push over them
# in every transport step, and mirrors their state into the
# MCNuX::mcnux_packet_diag table for golden output. Off by default — the
# fixture is verification scaffolding, not physics — and STEERABLE=NEVER,
# because the table's storage and the routines' scheduling are decided from
# it at startup.

BOOLEAN test_synthetic_packets "Seed the deterministic synthetic packet fixture and push it along geodesics each transport step" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Which deterministic seed set MCNuX_SeedSyntheticPackets writes (both are
# 8-row function-local tables in mcnux_geodesic.cxx, sized to the
# MCNuX::mcnux_packet_diag table): "minkowski" is the flat-spacetime set of
# the `minkowski-freestream` benchmark (|x^i| <= 0.25, six axis directions
# plus two oblique); "schwarzschild" is the curved-background set of the
# `schwarzschild-pt` drift/convergence legs (isotropic r in [6, 10] M,
# dominant outgoing-radial momenta). Ignored unless test_synthetic_packets =
# yes. STEERABLE=NEVER: the seed set is written once at initial time and
# golden data depends on it.

KEYWORD synthetic_packet_fixture "Deterministic seed set of the synthetic packet fixture" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  "minkowski"     :: "eight flat-spacetime packets inside |x^i| <= 0.25 (`minkowski-freestream`)"
  "schwarzschild" :: "eight outgoing packets at isotropic r in [6, 10] M (`schwarzschild-pt` legs)"
} "minkowski"

# Fluid-gather diagnostic switch of specs/neutrino-matter-interactions.md
# ([MCNX-INT-05] and the cell-centered u^mu of its inputs table; the
# `hydro-sphere-gather` benchmark): MCNuX::test_fluid_gather = yes schedules
# MCNuX_FluidGatherDiag, which reads the HydroBaseX (rho, vel, temperature,
# Ye) fields at every packet's containing cell (direct one-cell read, no
# interpolation), lifts v^i to u^mu on the cell-center metric, and mirrors
# the result into the MCNuX::mcnux_fluid_diag table for golden output. Off by
# default — the table is verification scaffolding, not physics — and
# STEERABLE=NEVER, because the table's storage and the routine's scheduling
# are decided from it at startup. Meaningful only together with
# test_synthetic_packets (without packets the table stays all-zero).

BOOLEAN test_fluid_gather "Mirror each packet's gathered cell-centered fluid state and four-velocity into the fluid-gather diagnostic table" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Transport-coefficient source of specs/opacity-eos-evaluation.md:118-124 and
# specs/verification-suite-design.md [MCNX-VER-05]: the production weaklib
# tables or the analytic (gray) Kirchhoff-form mode, both feeding the
# identical per-species coefficient interface (kappa_a, kappa_s, eta; g = 1)
# of src/mcnux_coefficients.hxx, so the switch is invisible below it. The
# analytic mode is a first-class physics capability (constant-opacity
# benchmarks, the nu_x coverage mechanism, the trapped-regime harness), not
# test scaffolding. STEERABLE=NEVER: consumers capture the source and its
# parameters once at startup.

KEYWORD opacity_source "Transport-coefficient source (specs/opacity-eos-evaluation.md:118-124, [MCNX-VER-05])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  "table"    :: "production weaklib tables"
  "analytic" :: "per-species gray Kirchhoff-form coefficients"
} "table"

# Analytic-mode coefficients, per species, indexed in the binding species
# order of specs/conventions-and-units.md:110-114: [0] = nu_e, [1] = nu_e_bar,
# [2] = nu_x (lumped heavy-lepton species). Formulas
# (specs/verification-suite-design.md:213-217, E and T in MeV):
#   kappa_a(s, E) = kappa_a0(s)
#   kappa_s(s, E) = kappa_s0(s)
#   eta(s, E)     = eta_scale(s) * c * kappa_a0(s) * 4 pi E^3/(hc)^3
#                   * 1/(exp(E/T) + 1)
# Non-negativity is enforced by the parameter ranges at parse time. Ignored
# unless opacity_source = "analytic".

CCTK_REAL kappa_a0[3] "Analytic-mode absorption opacity kappa_a0 per species [cm^-1]" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  0:* :: "non-negative"
} 0.0

CCTK_REAL kappa_s0[3] "Analytic-mode scattering opacity kappa_s0 per species [cm^-1]" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  0:* :: "non-negative"
} 0.0

CCTK_REAL eta_scale[3] "Analytic-mode emissivity scale eta_scale per species [dimensionless]: 1 = exact Kirchhoff equilibrium at mu_nu = 0, 0 = absorption-only medium" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  0:* :: "non-negative"
} 1.0

# Target packet fluid-frame energy of
# specs/packet-representation-and-sampling.md [MCNX-PKT-02]/[MCNX-PKT-03]:
# the emission count law N_p = g_s sqrt(-g) dV dt eta_b(s)/E_p creates
# packets of weight N = E_p/nu, so each packet carries fluid-frame energy E_p
# and E_p is the sole packet-count control pinned at baseline (per-region
# E_p, splitting, or rouletting would be a spec change). The spec pins no
# default; 10 MeV is a typical supernova-neutrino energy scale. STEERABLE=
# NEVER: the emission loop captures it once at startup, and mid-run changes
# would alter realized packet counts and golden data.

CCTK_REAL E_p "Target packet fluid-frame energy [MeV] (specs/packet-representation-and-sampling.md [MCNX-PKT-02])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  (0:* :: "positive target packet fluid-frame energy [MeV]"
} 10.0

# Production emission gate of specs/packet-representation-and-sampling.md
# [MCNX-PKT-02/03/05]: MCNuX::enable_emission = yes schedules MCNuX_Emission
# inside the transport step's MCNuX_AddToSourceTerms group, which runs the
# count law + creation loop over every cell, species, and energy bin,
# appends the created packets to the packet population, and deposits their
# emission ledger deltas into the source-term variables. Off by default —
# every pre-existing benchmark runs without the production population — and
# STEERABLE=NEVER, because the routine's scheduling is decided from it at
# startup. MCNuX_ParamCheck forbids it together with
# opacity_source = "table" (no table-residency layer yet) and with
# test_synthetic_packets (fixture ids would collide with production ids).

BOOLEAN enable_emission "Run the production emission/creation loop each transport step" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Episode-driver gate of specs/neutrino-matter-interactions.md
# [MCNX-INT-01/02/03/04/05/06]: MCNuX::enable_interactions = yes schedules
# MCNuX_EpisodeDriver inside the transport step (the MCNuX_GeodesicPush slot;
# the plain push is then NOT scheduled — the driver subsumes it), which runs
# the per-packet sampling-episode loop: interaction-time draws against
# cell-exit and step-remainder bounds, elastic scattering at fixed
# fluid-frame energy through the pinned tetrad transform, absorption
# removing the packet whole (full-content deposit, retired id, no weight
# decay), and every event's momentum/lepton exchange deposited into the
# source-term variables.
# Off by default and STEERABLE=NEVER, because the routine's scheduling is
# decided from it at startup. MCNuX_ParamCheck forbids it together with
# opacity_source = "table" (no table-residency layer yet); it IS compatible
# with test_synthetic_packets (the fixture is the test population of the
# `interactions-fixedseed` and `absorb-smoke` benchmarks).

BOOLEAN enable_interactions "Run the sampling-episode driver (interaction competition + elastic scattering) each transport step" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Trapped-regime scheme selector of specs/trapped-regime-treatment.md
# ([MCNX-TRP-01/02]; spec :81): "explicit" is the unmodified baseline (no
# relabeling anywhere — every pre-existing benchmark's golden data is a run
# of this branch); "relabeled" substitutes the primed coefficients
#   eta' = alpha eta, kappa_a' = alpha kappa_a,
#   kappa_s' = kappa_s + (1 - alpha) kappa_a
# (the BINDING 2021 alpha convention of [MCNX-TRP-03], mcnux_trp.hxx) into
# the emission count law and the event-sampling law — and nowhere else;
# tallies remain the actual packet events. alpha per (cell, species, energy
# bin) comes from the [MCNX-TRP-04] selection rule (trp_xi below) unless
# trp_alpha_fixed overrides it. STEERABLE=NEVER: the drivers capture the
# scheme once at startup (TrpParams of mcnux_trp.hxx). MCNuX_ParamCheck
# forbids "relabeled" with opacity_source = "table" (no table-residency
# layer exists, the enable_emission/enable_interactions precedent).

KEYWORD trapped_scheme "Trapped-regime treatment (specs/trapped-regime-treatment.md [MCNX-TRP-01/02])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  "explicit"  :: "unmodified coefficients (the baseline scheme)"
  "relabeled" :: "opacity relabeling with the [MCNX-TRP-04] alpha selection"
} "explicit"

# The xi control of the [MCNX-TRP-04] alpha-selection rule
# (specs/trapped-regime-treatment.md:145-171, provenance arXiv:2103.16588):
# alpha = min(1, xi/(kappa_a Dt_c)) per (cell, species, energy bin), with
# kappa_a the UNPRIMED code-unit absorption opacity and Dt_c the cell
# light-crossing time (min_d dx_d in code units, c = 1), so that
# kappa_a' Dt_c <= xi by construction — the only binding stability control
# (the beta-dependent Eq. 50 bound is an explicitly deferred open question,
# spec :450-455). Typically xi = 1 (the spec's stated practice). Ignored
# unless trapped_scheme = "relabeled", or when trp_alpha_fixed overrides the
# rule. STEERABLE=NEVER: captured once at startup.

CCTK_REAL trp_xi "Relabeled-scheme stability control xi of alpha = min(1, xi/(kappa_a Dt_c)) (specs/trapped-regime-treatment.md [MCNX-TRP-04])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  (0:* :: "positive stability control"
} 1.0

# Fixed-alpha verification override of specs/trapped-regime-treatment.md
# [MCNX-TRP-04]/[MCNX-TRP-05]: a value in (0, 1] replaces the selection rule
# with that constant alpha everywhere (alpha = 1 is the exact-identity
# endpoint the [MCNX-TRP-05] bitwise limit benchmark pins); the default -1
# sentinel selects the rule. The (0, 1] range clause IS the corpus's
# alpha-range rejection (spec :443-449; Cactus enforces parameter ranges at
# parse time). Ignored unless trapped_scheme = "relabeled". STEERABLE=NEVER:
# captured once at startup.

CCTK_REAL trp_alpha_fixed "Fixed-alpha override of the [MCNX-TRP-04] selection rule (-1 = use the rule; verification use, [MCNX-TRP-05])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  -1:-1 :: "sentinel: use the alpha-selection rule"
  (0:1] :: "fixed retained-fraction alpha (2021 convention, [MCNX-TRP-03])"
} -1.0

# Runtime id-contract check of specs/particle-container-and-gpu.md
# [MCNX-GPU-04] (the `absorb-smoke` benchmark): MCNuX::test_id_contract =
# yes schedules MCNuX_IdContractCheck once per transport step after the
# episode driver, sampling every live packet's id and asserting the id
# contract over the whole run — live logical keys pairwise distinct, ids in
# [1, 2^39 - 3], bit 63 of the repacked logical key (cpu << 39) | id clear,
# and no retired id value ever reappearing after a removal. Any violation is
# a hard CCTK_VERROR abort; the check writes no grid data. Off by default —
# verification scaffolding — and STEERABLE=NEVER, because the routine's
# scheduling is decided from it at startup.

BOOLEAN test_id_contract "Assert the [MCNX-GPU-04] packet id contract (uniqueness, range, bit 63, no retired-id reuse) every transport step" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Escape-tally diagnostic switch of specs/particle-container-and-gpu.md
# [MCNX-GPU-05] (the `escape-freestream` benchmark): MCNuX::
# test_escape_tallies = yes turns on storage for the
# MCNuX::mcnux_escape_diag table and schedules MCNuX_EscapeDiag once per
# transport step (plus an AT initial zero-baseline leg), mirroring the
# run-cumulative per-species escape tallies (packet count, number Sum N,
# energy Sum N p^t) into the table for golden output. The escape
# detection/tally/removal at the geodesic-push and episode-driver
# Redistribute sites is ALWAYS ON (binding correctness, not scaffolding) —
# this switch gates only the diagnostic surface. Off by default —
# verification scaffolding — and STEERABLE=NEVER, because the table's
# storage and the routine's scheduling are decided from it at startup.

BOOLEAN test_escape_tallies "Mirror the run-cumulative per-species escape tallies into the escape diagnostic table" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Emission diagnostic switch (the `emit-smoke` benchmark): MCNuX::
# test_emission = yes schedules MCNuX_EmissionDiag after MCNuX_Emission,
# mirroring the created packet population into the MCNuX::mcnux_packet_diag
# table (row = packet id - 1; the table's declared SIZE bounds the total
# emitted count, enforced by a hard error). Off by default — verification
# scaffolding — and STEERABLE=NEVER (storage and scheduling decided at
# startup). Meaningful only together with enable_emission.

BOOLEAN test_emission "Mirror the emitted packet population into the packet diagnostic table" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Statistical-reduction writer switch of specs/verification-suite-design.md
# [MCNX-VER-07] and specs/packet-representation-and-sampling.md [MCNX-PKT-06]
# (the `stats-emission` benchmark): MCNuX::test_stats_emission = yes turns on
# the step-scoped emission statistics accumulator inside MCNuX_Emission and
# schedules MCNuX_StatsEmission after it, reducing the emission step into
# per-check (estimate, expected, sigma, z) rows — per-species realized count,
# emitted energy (incl. the nu_x g = 4 leg), cos(theta)/phi first moments,
# plus the two RNG uniformity-at-the-pinned-bar rows — mirrored into the
# MCNuX::mcnux_stats_diag table for golden output. Off by default —
# verification scaffolding — and STEERABLE=NEVER, because the table's storage
# and the routine's scheduling are decided from it at startup. MCNuX_ParamCheck
# forbids it without enable_emission (there is no emission step to reduce).

BOOLEAN test_stats_emission "Reduce the emission step into (estimate, expected, sigma, z) statistical check rows" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Beam-attenuation benchmark switch of specs/neutrino-matter-interactions.md
# ([MCNX-INT-01]/[MCNX-INT-03] Verification: beam attenuation, statistical,
# 4 sigma) and specs/verification-suite-design.md [MCNX-VER-07] (the
# `stats-beam` benchmark): MCNuX::test_stats_beam = yes seeds the
# deterministic collimated monoenergetic beam at initial time
# (MCNuX_SeedBeamPackets: beam_num_packets nu_e packets at the seed plane
# beam_x0 with identical +x null momenta, no RNG consumed), turns on storage
# for the MCNuX::mcnux_stats_beam_diag verdict table, and schedules
# MCNuX_StatsBeam after the episode driver, reducing the run into the
# transmitted-count-vs-exp(-kappa_a L) check row and the exact count-closure
# row. Off by default — verification scaffolding — and STEERABLE=NEVER,
# because the table's storage and the routines' scheduling are decided from
# it at startup. MCNuX_ParamCheck requires enable_interactions with it (the
# episode driver IS the absorber) and forbids it with enable_emission and
# test_synthetic_packets (id-collision / duplicate-seeder hazards).

BOOLEAN test_stats_beam "Seed the deterministic beam fixture and reduce the run into the beam-attenuation statistical check rows" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Beam fixture controls (ignored unless test_stats_beam = yes; all
# STEERABLE=NEVER — the fixture is written once at initial time and golden
# data depends on it). The packet-count default is the pinned statistical
# N_p = 2^20 of [MCNX-RNG-07] (stats_default_num_packets, mcnux_stats.hxx);
# a benchmark pinning a different value documents it in its parfile.

CCTK_INT beam_num_packets "Number of beam packets (default: the pinned statistical N_p = 2^20 of [MCNX-RNG-07])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  1:* :: "at least one packet"
} 1048576

CCTK_REAL beam_energy_MeV "Beam packet energy [MeV] (monoenergetic; the attenuation law is energy-independent for gray kappa_a0)" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  (0:* :: "positive beam energy [MeV]"
} 10.0

CCTK_REAL beam_x0 "Seed-plane x coordinate of the beam [code units]; the slab thickness is L = x_hi - beam_x0" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  *:* :: "must lie inside the domain (checked at seeding; keep it off the x_lo face)"
} -0.875

# Scattering-collision-statistics benchmark switch of
# specs/neutrino-matter-interactions.md ([MCNX-INT-02]/[MCNX-INT-04]
# Verification: collision statistics + scattering isotropy, statistical,
# 4 sigma) and specs/verification-suite-design.md [MCNX-VER-07] (the
# `stats-scatterbox` benchmark): MCNuX::test_stats_scatterbox = yes seeds the
# deterministic cell-center packet lattice inside the inner cube
# [-scatterbox_half_width, +scatterbox_half_width]^3 at initial time
# (MCNuX_SeedScatterboxPackets: scatterbox_num_packets nu_e packets with
# identical +x null momenta, no RNG consumed), turns on the step-scoped
# scattering-statistics accumulator inside MCNuX_EpisodeDriver, turns on
# storage for the MCNuX::mcnux_stats_scatterbox_diag verdict table, and
# schedules MCNuX_StatsScatterbox after the episode driver, reducing the run
# into the Poisson mean/variance rows, the post-scatter isotropy rows, and
# the exact packets-sampled closure row. Off by default — verification
# scaffolding — and STEERABLE=NEVER, because the table's storage and the
# routines' scheduling are decided from it at startup. MCNuX_ParamCheck
# requires enable_interactions with it (the episode driver IS the scatterer)
# and forbids it with enable_emission, test_synthetic_packets, AND
# test_stats_beam (all other packet producers/seeders are id-collision /
# duplicate-seeder hazards: this seeder writes hard-coded ids 1..N with
# cpu 0).

BOOLEAN test_stats_scatterbox "Seed the deterministic scattering-box lattice and reduce the run into the collision-statistics check rows" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
} "no"

# Scatterbox fixture controls (ignored unless test_stats_scatterbox = yes;
# all STEERABLE=NEVER — the fixture is written once at initial time and
# golden data depends on it). The packet-count default is the pinned
# statistical N_p = 2^20 of [MCNX-RNG-07] (stats_default_num_packets,
# mcnux_stats.hxx); a benchmark pinning a different value documents it in
# its parfile.

CCTK_INT scatterbox_num_packets "Number of scatterbox packets (default: the pinned statistical N_p = 2^20 of [MCNX-RNG-07])" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  1:* :: "at least one packet"
} 1048576

CCTK_REAL scatterbox_energy_MeV "Scatterbox packet energy [MeV] (monoenergetic; the Poisson count law is energy-independent for gray kappa_s0)" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  (0:* :: "positive packet energy [MeV]"
} 10.0

CCTK_REAL scatterbox_half_width "Half-width h of the seeding cube [-h, h]^3 [code units]; must be strictly inside the domain (checked at seeding), and h + c dt below the domain half-width keeps the run escape-free by construction" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  (0:* :: "positive half-width [code units]"
} 0.4

# The run's base RNG seed S of specs/rng-and-reproducibility.md: every
# emission draw is an evaluation of the pure u(S, q, e, k) of mcnux_rng.hxx
# at this S. The default is the pinned primary statistics seed
# stats_seed_primary of mcnux_stats.hxx (1296518744 = 0x4D474E58), so runs
# are deterministic out of the box. STEERABLE=NEVER: the seed is captured
# once at startup and mid-run changes would break the (S, q, e, k) audit.

CCTK_INT rng_seed "Base RNG seed S of the pure counter-based draw function u(S, q, e, k)" STEERABLE=NEVER
{
  0:* :: "any non-negative 32-bit seed"
} 1296518744

# Single-rate pin of specs/carpetx-thorn-integration.md [MCNX-CTX-06]: MCNuX
# reads the driver's subcycling switch so that MCNuX_ParamCheck can abort a
# run configured with CarpetX::use_subcycling = yes. The CarpetX driver thorn
# IMPLEMENTS: Driver, so the sharing block targets the capability name Driver
# (the live idiom of CarpetX/ODESolvers/param.ccl).

SHARES: Driver

USES BOOLEAN use_subcycling
